         "children": [
          {
           "t": "heading",
           "level": "h2",
           "text": "What Makes a Logo Work for an Austin Business?",
           "classes": []
          },
          {
           "t": "text",
           "html": "<p>A strong logo is <strong>simple, memorable and versatile</strong>. It must stay legible on a phone screen and an embroidered hat, work in one color, and signal the right tone for the industry: a law firm usually needs a restrained serif mark, while a food truck or apparel brand can be bold and playful.</p><p>Logo Austin designers also consider where the logo will appear first. A contractor's logo has to read on a truck door from across a parking lot; a boutique's logo has to look good on a shopping bag and an Instagram profile.</p>",
           "classes": []
          }
         ]
        }
       ]
      }
     ]
    }
